The city administrator shall be the chief administrative officer of the city and position may be combined with the office of city clerk or may be two separate positions occupied by two separate individuals. The city administrator shall be responsible to the city council for the administration of all city affairs placed in the city administrator's charge by or under this charter. The city administrator:
(1) Shall direct and supervise the administration of all departments, offices and agencies of the city, except as otherwise provided by this charter or by law;
(2) Shall attend all city council meetings and shall have the right to take part in discussion, but the city administrator may not vote;
(3) Shall see that all laws, provisions of this charter, and acts of the city council, subject to enforcement by the city administrator or by officers subject to the city administrator's direction and supervision, are faithfully executed;
(4) Shall prepare and submit the annual operating budget and capital budget to the city council.
(5) Shall submit to the city council and make available to the public a complete report on the finances and administrative activities of the city as of the end of each fiscal year;
(6) Shall make other such reports as the city council may require concerning the operations of city departments, offices, and agencies subject to the city administrator's direction and supervisions;
(7) Shall keep the city council fully advised as to the financial condition and future needs of the city, and make such recommendations to the city council concerning the affairs of the city as the city administrator deems desirable; and
(8) Shall perform other such duties as are specified in this charter or as may be required by the city council.
(Ord. No. 373, 7-14-2009)

